.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_STREAM_COUNT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_stream_count
.Nd count the records at each time
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_count "dtfl_stream *st"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_stream_count
produces a stream of record counts.
For each distinct time at which
.Fa st
carries records, the operator accumulates the number of records seen,
and emits that count as a single
.Vt uint64_t
record once the input frontier has passed the time, so the count is
complete before it is reported.
The output stream carries
.Fn dtfl_type_u64
records.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_stream_count
returns the count stream, owned by the scope.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_stream *counts = dtfl_stream_count(in);
counts = dtfl_stream_inspect(counts, print_count, DTFL_NOCTX);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn dtfl_stream_count
does not return an error code.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_stream_concat 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_exchange 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_map 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_partition 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_to_stream 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
This is the C form of timely's
.Fn count
operator, part of the
.Fn Accumulate
trait at the 0.31 pin.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
The operator and its stream belong to the worker thread that built
them and must not be shared.
